Ladybird’s tabs.onUpdated reports what changed among a tab’s status,
URL, title, and pin, with the URL and title only when the extension may
see them, as Chromium’s TabsEventRouter does (it strips them without the
tabs permission or a host permission), and as Gecko’s ext-tabs.js and
WebKit’s WebExtensionContextAPITabsCocoa.mm do too. A private tab’s
events reach only extensions allowed in private windows, as in all
three. But Ladybird doesn’t report favIconUrl yet, which all three do.
